    "notes": [
      {
        "category": "summary",
        "text": "An update is available for c-ares.\nThis update affects Rocky Linux 8.\nA Common Vulnerability Scoring System (CVSS) base score, which gives a detailed severity rating, is available for each vulnerability from the CVE list",
        "title": "Topic"
      },
      {
        "category": "description",
        "text": "The c-ares C library defines asynchronous DNS (Domain Name System) requests and provides name resolving API.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* c-ares: Heap buffer over read in ares_parse_soa_reply (CVE-2020-22217)\n\n* c-ares: Buffer Underwrite in ares_inet_net_pton() (CVE-2023-31130)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.\n\nThis advisory is provided by Ctrl IQ, Inc for Rocky Linux systems. For more information about CIQ security practices, visit https://ciq.com/security.",
        "title": "Description"
      },
      {
        "category": "legal_disclaimer",
        "text": "This content is licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). If you distribute this content, or a modified version of it, you must provide attribution to the original copyright holder(s) and provide a link to the original.",
